# Keep the devcontainer/Dockerfile build context small and avoid baking
# host-local state (venvs, caches, secrets, agent scratch) into the image.
#
# ALLOWLIST, not a denylist. This is a shared factory worktree: concurrent
# agents leave dozens of untracked `tmp-*` probe trees, plus `scratch/`,
# `logs/`, `bucket/` and a 15 GB `var/` at the repo root. A
# denylist silently re-admits every new one — the previous denylist shipped a
# 1.12 GB context that took 53 s to transfer on every build. Ignoring
# everything and re-admitting the build's real inputs keeps the context small
# without maintenance.
#
# The devcontainer bind-mounts the live workspace over /workspace at runtime
# (see .devcontainer/devcontainer.json `workspaceMount`), so what is copied
# here only has to satisfy the image-build pre-warm and `just
# devcontainer-test`: the dependency install, `import cadrumo`, and unit-test
# collection over the `testpaths` declared in pyproject.toml
# (`src/cadrumo` plus `dev/packaging/tests/test_installed_oracles.py`).
*

# -- Project metadata the install resolves from ------------------------------
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!.python-version
!README.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!justfile
!conftest.py

# -- Source, dev lanes, and the two path-sourced data companions -------------
# `packaging/` carries cadrumo-data-{manuals,official}, declared as
# `[tool.uv.sources]` path dependencies; their hatch build hooks force-include
# from `src/cadrumo/_data/corpus`, so both trees are install-time inputs.
!src
!dev
!packaging
!env

# -- Noise inside the admitted trees ----------------------------------------
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[codz]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov
**/*.log
**/var
env/.env
